+# Develop and release Google Guide Skills
+
+This document contains maintainer commands and generated-output rules. Users installing skills do
+not need these steps.
+
+## Prepare the repository
+
+The package and unit tests support Python 3.11+. Byte-for-byte generation is pinned to Python
+3.13.7 in `.python-version` and `corpus.yaml`; `uv` provisions that interpreter.
+
+```bash
+uv sync --all-groups
+uv run google-guides all
+```
+
+`google-guides all` checks out pinned sources, builds the public skill set, regenerates the
+catalog and token report, and validates the result. Use `--include-swe-book` for a local release
+check that also materializes the restricted book output.
+
+## Run presubmit checks
+
+```bash
+uv run ruff format --check src tests
+uv run ruff check .
+uv run pytest --cov=google_guide_skills --cov-report=term-missing
+uv run google-guides all
+git diff --exit-code -- skills catalog
+```
+
+Hosted CI uses synthetic restricted-source fixtures and never materializes the real Software
+Engineering at Google derivatives.
+
+## Change the corpus
+
+Update `corpus.yaml` or the generator, then regenerate. Keep tests, generated outputs, and license
+evidence in the same change. Never add a source whose distribution rights are unclear.
+
+The project is marked `Private :: Do Not Upload`. Wheels exclude generated guide trees and do not
+contain an initialized corpus.
+
+For command details, run `uv run google-guides --help`. See the [architecture](architecture.md),
+[evaluation guide](evaluation.md), and [source licensing policy](licensing.md) for the relevant
+maintainer contracts.
